# Implementation Plan — Hybrid Dense + Sparse Retrieval System

This implementation plan details the architecture and components required to build the hybrid retrieval system in `com.medisense.rag.retrieval`.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **HyDE (Hypothetical Document Embeddings)**: Uses Gemini Flash to generate a hypothetical clinical guideline sentence before embedding, with a robust fallback to direct query embedding if the LLM call fails.
> - **Dense pgvector Retrieval**: Cosine similarity search (`<=>`) over 768-dim embeddings with metadata pre-filtering (`is_active = TRUE`, `evidence_basis`, `domain_tags`).
> - **Sparse Lucene BM25 Retrieval**: Local `FSDirectory` BM25 search over active child chunks with score normalization to $[0, 1]$.
> - **Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)**: Merges dense top-20 and sparse top-20 using $\text{score} = \frac{1}{60 + \text{dense\_rank}} + \frac{1}{60 + \text{sparse\_rank}}$ (missing rank default: 21).
> - **Parallel Execution**: `RetrievalOrchestrator` executes dense and sparse searches concurrently via `CompletableFuture`.
> - **Parent Chunk Fetcher**: Retrieves full section-level parent context for the top-selected child chunks.

